llama.cpp 8c2134a8755d8a9792af513dab20282affe903e4 (2026-10-14)

Only the ggml files that the GGUF ops (freetoken/ggml_ops.cu, built by kernel/ggml.py) compile or include:
ggml/include -> include, ggml/src -> src, ggml/src/ggml-cuda -> ggml-cuda.

Local changes, kept in freetoken.patch (already applied):
- quantize.cu/.cuh: the q8_1 quantize kernels read fp32, bf16 or fp16 activations.
- mmq.cu/.cuh: MMQ takes bf16 or fp16 activations, except on the native fp4 path. Its kernels are built for fp32 and bf16 results (dst_t); a bf16 result that needs the stream-k fixup is computed in fp32 first, and so is an fp16 result unless GGML_MMQ_F16_DST builds fp16 kernels too.
- mmvq.cu/.cuh: MMVQ takes bf16 or fp16 activations, can write bf16 or fp16 results, and can reuse activations already quantized to q8_1 (src1_q8_1_pre).
- mmq.cu/.cuh, mmid.cu/.cuh: MoE MMQ runs a flat grid over only the (expert, column tile) pairs that hold tokens, listed by mm_ids_tile_map; ncols_max > 0 keeps the regular grid.
- common.cuh: the native fp4 MMA (BLACKWELL_MMA_AVAILABLE, blackwell_mma_available) is off unless GGML_CUDA_FP4_MMA is defined; it needs an sm_120a/sm_120f build.

To update: copy the same files from a newer llama.cpp, apply freetoken.patch, and update this file.
